{"content":"Found the bug: `TokenList.insert_after` in sqlparse/sql.py has inverted logic. When `next_` is not None it should insert the token at `nidx`, but currently it appends to the end of the list; when `next_` is None it should append, but currently it tries to insert at `nidx` (which would be None). This explains the misaligned CASE/aligned-indent output, since `aligned_indent.py`'s `_process_case` calls `tlist.insert_after(cond[-1], ws)` to insert whitespace right after a condition token when there's more following (THEN) — with the inverted bug this gets appended at the very end instead, breaking alignment of CASE statements and other aligned-indent formatting that relies on insert_after/insert_before behavior.

